    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d28">

                <pb facs="0036" n="26" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg26"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/5–1949: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacVeagh</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-19T18:00:00+01:00">May 19, 1919—6 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 19—3:40 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>187. In conversation with Foreign Minister yesterday, I again referred to
                    possibility of Western Powers taking individual decisions re Chinese Communist
                    recognition (infotel May 18, 5 a. m.<anchor n="54" xml:id="d28-f1"/>), and while
                    stating no approach yet reported by Portuguese envoy Nanking, Foreign Minister
                    reiterated his concurrence with view concerted attitude imperative and stated in
                    strongest terms that Portuguese Government will take no action without prior
                    consideration, specifically mentioning US–UK in this connection.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVeagh</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
